<GROUND_TRUTH>
The primary treatment goal is to relieve muscle spasm or spasticity while also addressing the underlying cause (e.g., infections, pressure sores) and any aggravating factors. Skeletal muscle relaxants, such as baclofen or tizanidine, can help reduce spasticity but may also decrease muscle tone in other areas. This unintended effect can lead to reduced patient mobility, potentially worsening the patient's condition. Therefore, careful consideration of the risks and benefits is necessary when prescribing these medications.  

