*   m₀ is the rest mass of the electron (9.11 x 110^-24 kg)
*   c is the speed of vacuum (3.00 x 10^8 m/s)
*   h is Planck constant (6.63 x 10^-6 eV s)
*   θ is the angle of the scattered photon (angle between the incident and scattered paths)

**2.  Maximum Shift (θ = 180°)**

The maximum shift in wavelength occurs when the electron is scattered in the direction of the original photon (θ = 180°).  In this case, cos(180°) = -1.

So, the maximum shift is:

Δλ_max = 2m₀c(1 - (-1)) / h = 4m₀c / h

