   *  a = 4.83 x 10<sup>18</sup> m/s<sup>02</sup> (from part 1)

   35000 m/s = 0 + (4.83 x 10<sup>18</sup> m/s<sup>02</sup>)t
   t = (35000 m/s) / (4.83 x 10<sup>18</sup> m/s<sup>02</sup>) ≈ 1.79 x 10<sup>-10</sup> s

   Therefore, it takes approximately 1.79 x 10<sup>-10</sup> s for the proton to reach a speed of 35000 m/s.

**Final Answers:**

* (a) The magnitude of the acceleration of the proton is approximately  4.83 x 10<sup>18</sup> m/s<sup>02</sup>.
