   \]

3. **Total entropy change**:
   The total entropy increase of the combined system is the sum of the entropy changes of the water and the gas:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{total}} = \Delta S_{\text{water}} + \Delta S_{\text{gas}} = 3.77 - 1.725 = 2.045 \text{ kJ/K}.
   \]

Thus, the total entropy of the combined system increases by \(\boxed{2.045 \text{ kJ/K}}\).
